.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt PRINTF 3
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm printf
.Nm fprintf
.Nm sprintf
.Nm snprintf
.Nm dprintf
.Nm vprintf
.Nd formatted output
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In stdio.h
.Ft int
.Fn printf "const char *format" ...
.Ft int
.Fn fprintf "FILE *stream" "const char *format" ...
.Ft int
.Fn sprintf "char *buffer" "const char *format" ...
.Ft int
.Fn snprintf "char *buffer" "size_t size" "const char *format" ...
.Ft int
.Fn dprintf "int fd" "const char *format" ...
.Ft int
.Fn vprintf "const char *format" "va_list ap"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These functions format their arguments and write the result to a stream, a descriptor or a
buffer. The conversion set follows ISO C23 and the POSIX additions implemented by ravenlibc.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The functions return the number of bytes that would have been written, or a negative value on
failure. .Fn snprintf truncates the output to the supplied size but returns the untruncated length.
.Sh ERRORS
.Er EINVAL is returned for a malformed conversion. Output errors are reported with
.Er EIO, .Er ENOSPC or .Er EBADF as appropriate for the destination.
.Sh STANDARDS
ISO C23 and POSIX.1-2024; ring 0.
.Sh CAVEATS
The %n conversion stores the count in the default build and aborts in the hardened profile.
The %m conversion is supported. See H-6 and C43.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr printf 3
.Xr stdio 3
